    ["Counting letters instead of sounds (ship has three sounds).", "Guessing a spelling instead of choosing a strategy.", "Forgetting the adding rules: hope + ing is hoping, hop + ing is hopping.", "Skipping the Check step of Look, Say, Cover, Write, Check."],
    [{"title": "Word Wall", "description": "Make a word wall of 10 tricky words with the tricky part in a different colour.", "type": "create", "difficulty": "medium", "evidence_type": "photo"},
     {"title": "Spelling Teacher", "description": "Teach a family member one strategy using three words and ask them to spell each one.", "type": "speak", "difficulty": "medium", "evidence_type": "audio"}],
    "Part A: ele-phant 3 (el-e-phant), ad-ven-ture 3, won-der-ful 3, un-der-stand 3. Part B: re + play + ing; un + happy + ly (happily, y to i); mis + spell + ing; care + ful + ly. Part C: hoping, hopping, happiness, carried, careless. Part D (suggested): said, because: LSCWC and a memory trick; favourite: syllables fav-our-ite; beautiful: syllables beau-ti-ful or beauty + ful.",
