    "1) My sister can't swim, but she loves the beach. 2) We saw a seal, a penguin and a whale at the zoo. 3) After lunch, we went to the park. It was hot. (or ...park, and it was hot.) 4) Is that your dog's ball? (ownership: dog's ball; the apostrophe of possession is an extension) 5) Running down the hill is a fragment: add a subject, e.g. The boy was running down the hill. 6) The bird flapped its wings, and it's time to fly. Sentence types: any correct statement, question, command and exclamation.",
